  "description": "meme-id: brick_wall_with_hole; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a brick wall with a missing section, visually representing a gap or void. The text \"when i try to fit in with other people\" suggests the meme is conveying the emotional or psychological experience of feeling like one doesn't belong or is unable to integrate into a social group. The overall intent is to express a relatable feeling of alienation or social exclusion. While the meme does not contain explicit hate, abuse, or harmful stereotypes targeting specific protected groups, it does convey a potentially painful emotional state that could be harmful to individuals who experience social isolation or struggle with fitting in. The visual metaphor of the hole in the wall effectively maps onto the textual message, illustrating the 'gap' or 'missing piece' one feels when trying to belong. The intent is not to attack or demean any group, but to communicate a personal, universal human experience of social disconnection, which can be emotionally taxing and may resonate with those who feel marginalized or out of place.",
